# Implementation Plan: Allen Neuropixels Neural Dynamics

This plan outlines the steps and architecture to build a prototype model of neural population dynamics using the Allen Brain Observatory Visual Coding dataset, predicting VISp regional activity.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> - Should I create the project in `c:/Users/shafi/OneDrive/Documents/DDM/allen_neural_dynamics`?
> - The dataset download (even for one session) using AllenSDK can take several gigabytes. I will set it to save to `data/raw/`. Is this acceptable?

## Proposed Changes

### Project Structure & Configuration
- Create `c:/Users/shafi/OneDrive/Documents/DDM/allen_neural_dynamics`
#### [NEW] `requirements.txt`
Includes `allensdk`, `torch`, `pandas`, `numpy`, `matplotlib`, `scikit-learn`, `pyyaml`, `jupyter`.
#### [NEW] `config/default.yaml`
Contains all configurable hyperparameters: session_id, region, bin_size, stimulus handling, model types, hidden dims, dt, learning_rate, epochs, batch_size.

---
### Codebase (`src/`)
#### [NEW] `src/data_access.py`
Sets up the AllenSDK cache, lists and downlaods a selected session. Robust against missing caches.
#### [NEW] `src/preprocessing.py`
Extracts units for the specified region (default `VISp`), bins spike times to create population trace `x(t)` (using mean firing rate), and smooths it using a standard Gaussian filter.
#### [NEW] `src/features.py`
Aligns the visual stimulus presentation table to the same time bins to create a binary input trace `u(t)`.
#### [NEW] `src/datasets.py`
Creates a PyTorch `Dataset` that takes `x(t)`, `u(t)` to predict `x(t+1)`. Splits the timeline into first 70% train, 15% validation, and last 15% test.
#### [NEW] `src/models.py`
Implements:
1. `PersistenceBaseline`: returns `x(t)` as prediction.
2. `LinearBaseline` / `MLPBaseline`: uses `[x(t), u(t)]` -> `x(t+1)`.
3. `MechanisticModel`: Wilson-Cowan-inspired discrete update of `E(t)` and `I(t)`, mapping `E(t)` to `x_hat`.
4. `HybridModel`: `MechanisticModel` with a small additive MLP residual correction.
#### [NEW] `src/train.py` & `src/utils.py`
Training loop with early stopping, model checkpointing, evaluating MSE and saving metrics.
#### [NEW] `src/evaluate.py`
Tests models on the test split, computing MSE, MAE, Pearson, and R2.
#### [NEW] `src/visualize.py`
Generates plots: 1) True vs. Predicted sample window with aligned stimulus, 2) Train/val loss curves.
#### [NEW] `run_experiment.py`
The main entry script parsing `config/default.yaml` to run end-to-end.
#### [NEW] `notebooks/exploration.ipynb`
Jupyter notebook to interactively fetch data, visualize subsets of VISp spikes, and plot `x(t)` and `u(t)`.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- Running `python run_experiment.py` should successfully produce test metrics, models, and figures in the `outputs/` folder.
### Manual Verification
- Reviewing `exploration.ipynb` to visually confirm valid extraction of `VISp` spikes and sensible `x(t)` / `u(t)` alignment.
- Checking `outputs/figures/` to confirm that predictions reasonably track ground truth traces compared to the persistence baseline.
